About Boots

Join a business that combines a rich heritage with a bold vision for the future. At Boots, you'll be part of a team that touches the lives of millions of people every week, helping customers feel healthier, happier, and more confident. Whether you're driving innovation behind the scenes or delivering exceptional experiences directly to customers, you'll play a role in shaping one of the UK's most recognised and trusted brands.

You'll work in an environment that values collaboration, fresh thinking, and continuous learning. No two days are the same. One day you could be solving complex challenges, the next launching new initiatives that improve customer experiences or drive business growth. You'll be supported by talented colleagues who are passionate about what they do and committed to helping each other succeed.

As a business operating across retail, healthcare, digital, technology, supply chain and corporate functions, Boots offers opportunities to work on projects at scale while maintaining a strong sense of purpose and community. It's a place where ideas are welcomed, development is encouraged, and individuals are empowered to make a meaningful contribution.

This is more than just a job. It's an opportunity to build a career with impact, work with great people, and be part of a business that continues to evolve, innovate, and make a difference in communities across the UK.

Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

Managing&nbsp;Partner &nbsp;

About the role: &nbsp;

Are you passionate about clients and their business, leading teams to create unrivalled work that grows our client’s business and builds long term relationships with them?&nbsp;&nbsp;

Boots&nbsp;is looking for an ambitious Managing Partner to join our Client Leadership Community - the voice of our clients in the agency.&nbsp;

As the voice of the client across the agency, we’re focused on ensuring our clients&nbsp;will&nbsp;have their best agency experience during their time with Boots&nbsp;

We’re looking for someone who can inspire clients and teams to create unrivalled work, help define the ways of working across the agency that deliver the best client experiences, and in turn grow our relationships with existing and potential new clients.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

In this role, you will: &nbsp;

• Be responsible for the output delivered to the client across all contact points.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• You will have a deep understanding of all elements of a client’s business, the category and industry in which they operate and use this knowledge to help deliver the client vision for growth.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Working with all specialists you will be able to connect with stakeholders across the client’s business, who may sit outside of your day-to-day team.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• You will understand where the client sits in the client life
